Make diff -B count a line of only CR LF as empty.
Unless --binary is given, diff ignores a CR before an LF when it
compares lines, so a CR LF file and the same text with LF endings are
equal. But -B decided that a changed line was empty by its length
alone, one octet, so an inserted or deleted blank line in a CR LF file
still made a hunk, and -B was useless on such files. When -B and the
CR handling are in effect, also treat a two-octet line that is CR LF
as empty.

---
 editors/diff.c |   19 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/editors/diff.c
+++ b/editors/diff.c
@@ -668,8 +668,23 @@
 				}
 
 				for (j = 0; j < 2; j++)
-					for (k = v[j].a; k <= v[j].b; k++)
-						nonempty |= (ix[j][k] - ix[j][k - 1] != 1);
+					for (k = v[j].a; k <= v[j].b; k++) {
+						off_t len = ix[j][k] - ix[j][k - 1];
+#if ENABLE_PLATFORM_MINGW32 && ENABLE_FEATURE_DIFF_LONG_OPTIONS
+						/* -B: a lone CR LF is an empty line too */
+						if (len == 2 && (option_mask32 & FLAG(B))
+						 && !(option_mask32 & FLAG(binary))
+						) {
+							seek_ft(&ft[j], ix[j][k - 1]);
+							if (fgetc(ft[j].ft_fp) == '\r'
+							 && fgetc(ft[j].ft_fp) == '\n'
+							)
+								len = 1;
+							ft[j].ft_pos = -1; /* force the next seek */
+						}
+#endif
+						nonempty |= (len != 1);
+					}
 
 				vec = xrealloc_vector(vec, 6, ++idx);
 				memcpy(vec[idx], v, sizeof(v));
